d again the stronger the score for  experimental data the stronger  interaction  and then we have also a drug interaction  database with kinases  and what's unique about these maps is  that if you click on one of the  peripheral  components in the map it becomes the hub  of a new map  and shows you all its interacting  players so for example if you saw a drug  that's  the santa nib was strong effect on able  here you can click on this antenna and  it becomes the center of a hub and you  see all the associative proteins  so i apologize that the talk has gone  a little over  there's a lot to cover  there's a lot of people that are  responsible for allowing me to put this  data together and to create these  websites  and  i'm quite  grateful to them  i'm also thankful to the organizers for  the opportunity to present this work  and to you for taking the time of your  busy schedules to see what it is that  we're doing  i'll  take a few  questions  uh and the q a  section and if there's any questions  uh be happy to see them presently i  don't see any questions  so i guess  we can call that  the end of the session  and i  urge you to try to take a look at these  websites and to use them i think they're  very powerful  for designing experiments  and we have other websites that are in  development as well  uh one  on protein kinases another one that's a  a publication database where a lot of  the data i'm showing today will be in a  publishable format for you to refer to  so again thank you very much and uh  good luck with your own research  and goodbye  bye
 

